pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$bg"
elements:
  # ---------- header ----------
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 38, 700, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        SOLUTION 1 OF 2 — SEMANTIC LAYER · FIXES THE LOGIC
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 58, 720, 44]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        What is a semantic layer?
  - elementId: title-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 118, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- left column: definition + bullets ----------
  - elementId: definition
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 140, 470, 108]
    content:
      fontSize: 17.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>A <strong>governed layer of metric definitions</strong> between your data and everyone who consumes it — <strong>define each metric once</strong>, and every dashboard, spreadsheet, and AI agent works from the same number.</p>
  - elementId: bullets
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 262, 470, 206]
    content:
      fontSize: 12.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p><span style="color:$sl">■</span> <strong>Define once, use everywhere.</strong> One certified definition of a metric like Unbilled USD — not a slightly different formula in every report.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:11px"><span style="color:$sl">■</span> <strong>It translates; it doesn't copy.</strong> Definitions point at the data where it lives — nothing is moved or duplicated.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:11px"><span style="color:$sl">■</span> <strong>Versioned and reviewed like code.</strong> When a definition changes, every consumer changes with it.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:11px"><span style="color:$sl">■</span> <strong>Humans and AI agents get the same answer.</strong> An agent reads the approved metric instead of inventing its own SQL.</p>
  - elementId: bridge
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 484, 470, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p><span style="color:$ont">→</span> That fixes the logic — <strong><span style="color:$ont">not the meaning</span></strong>. Meaning is the ontology's job, next.</p>

  # ---------- right column: three-layer stack ----------
  - elementId: stack-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 136, 316, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.5
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        WHO ASKS
  # consumer chips
  - elementId: chip-1
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [580, 154, 100, 40]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$white"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: chip-1-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 154, 100, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      align: [center, middle]
      lineHeight: 1.25
      text: |
        Dashboards & BI
  - elementId: chip-2
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [688, 154, 100, 40]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$white"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: chip-2-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [688, 154, 100, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      align: [center, middle]
      lineHeight: 1.25
      text: |
        Spreadsheets
  - elementId: chip-3
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [796, 154, 100, 40]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$white"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: chip-3-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [796, 154, 100, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      align: [center, middle]
      lineHeight: 1.25
      text: |
        AI agents
  # arrows chips -> semantic band (question down, answer up)
  - elementId: arr-1
    elementType: line
    bounds: [629, 196, 2, 28]
    viewBox: [2, 28]
    points: "1,0 1,28"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [arrow, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$faint"}
  - elementId: arr-2
    elementType: line
    bounds: [737, 196, 2, 28]
    viewBox: [2, 28]
    points: "1,0 1,28"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [arrow, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$faint"}
  - elementId: arr-3
    elementType: line
    bounds: [845, 196, 2, 28]
    viewBox: [2, 28]
    points: "1,0 1,28"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [arrow, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$faint"}
  # semantic layer band
  - elementId: sl-band
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [580, 226, 316, 112]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$slSoft"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.5, color: "$sl"}
  - elementId: sl-band-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [596, 236, 284, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$sl"
      bold: true
      letterSpacing: 1.5
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        SEMANTIC LAYER
  - elementId: sl-band-sub
    elementType: text
    bounds: [596, 254, 284, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 12.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Definitions + rules, governed in one place
  - elementId: sl-band-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [596, 278, 284, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$slLine"}
  - elementId: sl-band-example
    elementType: text
    bounds: [596, 288, 284, 42]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$muted"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p><strong><span style="color:$ink">Example — Unbilled USD:</span></strong> sum of net gallons × contract price, delivered tickets with no posted invoice</p>
  # arrows semantic band -> data band
  - elementId: arr-4
    elementType: line
    bounds: [629, 338, 2, 22]
    viewBox: [2, 22]
    points: "1,0 1,22"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [arrow, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$faint"}
  - elementId: arr-5
    elementType: line
    bounds: [737, 338, 2, 22]
    viewBox: [2, 22]
    points: "1,0 1,22"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [arrow, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$faint"}
  - elementId: arr-6
    elementType: line
    bounds: [845, 338, 2, 22]
    viewBox: [2, 22]
    points: "1,0 1,22"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [arrow, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$faint"}
  # data band
  - elementId: data-band
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [580, 360, 316, 56]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$white"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: data-band-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [596, 368, 284, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.5
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        DATA
  - elementId: data-band-sub
    elementType: text
    bounds: [596, 384, 284, 24]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        Warehouse tables · operational systems — the data stays where it lives
  - elementId: analogy
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 434, 316, 52]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$muted"
      italic: true
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Like a restaurant menu: you order the dish — you don't need to know how the kitchen made it.</p>

  # ---------- footer ----------
  - elementId: footer-left
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 514, 560, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Anchor example: O2C unbilled exposure — from the EPM demo (fct_unbilled, one certified metric)
  - elementId: footer-right
    elementType: text
    bounds: [830, 514, 66, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [right, middle]
      text: |
        02 / 05
